C - ARRAYS
===========

Store multiple values of same type.


BASIC ARRAY
-----------
int numbers[5];          Array of 5 integers
numbers[0] = 10;         First element
numbers[4] = 50;         Last element (index 4)


INITIALIZATION
---------------
int arr[3] = {1, 2, 3};
int list[] = {10, 20, 30};   Size auto-detected
char name[10];               Empty array


ACCESS ELEMENTS
---------------
arr[0]     First element
arr[2]     Third element
arr[i]     Element at index i


LOOPS WITH ARRAYS
------------------
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    printf("%d\n", arr[i]);
}


MULTI-DIMENSIONAL
------------------
int matrix[3][3];           2D array (3x3)
matrix[0][0] = 5;           Row 0, Column 0
matrix[i][j];               Access element


COMMON USES
-----------
Store numbers
Store names
Store grades
Lookup tables


ERRORS
------
arr[10] for 5-element array → Out of bounds
Off-by-one errors → Common mistake
Uninitialized array → Garbage data


TIPS
----
Index starts at 0.
Last index is size - 1.
Bounds checking is your job.
